is or her saving throw against petrification for each such potential hit."],[41,0,2,44,47,3,"A42","When making saves against attacks, if save is successful will take no damage (e.g. from a fireball). At 9th level and above, even if save is failed, only take 1/2 damage."],[43,0,1,44,48,2,"A44","At 8th level gains folowers (PHB 32)"],[44,0,1,44,49,1,0,"Class Restrictions"],[45,0,3,44,47,3,"A46","1. A monk may possess no more than two magic weapons and three other magic items (see 3 below) at any time. While monks may retain money sufficient for their modest needs, and to support their henchmen (see 5 below), all other treasure and excess magic items must be bestowed upon (non player) religious institutions."],[48,0,2,44,47,3,"A49","2. Magic items usable by monks include all magical varieties of weapons listed (unless proscribed), rings, and those miscellaneous magic items which are usable by thieves. No other magic items of any sort may be employed by monks."],[50,0,2,34,50,3,"A51","3 Below 6th level no hirelings/henchmen. Starting at 6th level can get hirelings for 1 adventure and 2 henchmen (Fighter, Thieves or Assassins only) + 1 henchment for each level above 6th."],[50,34,1,10,15,1,0,"Max # Henchmen"],[51,34,1,10,51,3,"AI52"],[52,0,1,11,52,1,0,"Weapon"],[52,11,2,2,53,1,0,"hit\nadj."],[52,13,2,3,54,1,0,"magic\nadj."],[52,16,2,2,53,1,"Q53","dam.\nAdj.","Sums damage bonus from STR and \"magic adj.\"\nThis column value is automatically added to Damage columns to the right. So don't add it again."],[52,18,1,7,55,1,"S53","Damage","Includes the \"dam. adj\" from STR and \"magic adj.\""],[52,25,1,10,56,1,"Z53","AC adjustment","Only used whan an opponent is wearing armor. Each number corresponds to a specific armor type (i.e. magic armor does not change this).\n10 = no armor\n9 = Shield\n8 = Leather/Padded\n7 =  Leather/Padded + Shield or Studded / Ring-mail\n6 = Studded / Ring-mail + Shield or Scale mail\n5 = Scale mail + Shield or Chain mail\n4 = Chain mail + Shield or 